  "question": "Can exact capability bounds and a post-verifier scalar guard contain the same direct spatial effects under matched verifier defects and inputs?",
  "supported_result": "Both defenses contain all four tested direct map effects. Exact capability authority requires no per-access scalar guard; the test-only scalar comparator adds 40 native bytes per checked access plus one shared 8-byte failure stub.",
  "claim_limits": [
    "This is a functional and native-code-size comparison, not a runtime performance result.",
    "The scalar comparator is a narrow Morello hybrid, not portable SFI, AEE, or a production baseline.",
    "The component inventory exposes trust obligations; it does not prove that either total TCB is smaller.",
    "The experiment does not measure verifier state-space, latency, or maintenance complexity."
  ],
